      "id": 1,
      "text": "Blossom was originally called Blossom Prairie, a name shortened in 1888 as the town grew.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blossom%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1876 the settlement became a stop on the Texas and Pacific Railway, quickly turning into a shipping point for lumber, ties, livestock, and grain.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/blossom-tx"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By 1914 Blossom hosted a cottonseed oil mill, cotton gin, brickyard, produce company, and broom factory, showcasing a diverse local economy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/blossom-tx"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Blossom’s city motto emphasizes small‑town values, guided growth, and the preservation of its historical, cultural, and natural heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.blossomtexas.gov/"
    },
    {
